+# android_device_oppo_sm8250-common
+
+Common device tree for OPPO/realme **SM8250 (kona)** devices, used by
+[`device/realme/rivena`](https://github.com/RMX3366-Development/android_device_realme_rivena).
+
+> Fork of [RMX3366-Development/android_device_oppo_sm8250-common](https://github.com/RMX3366-Development/android_device_oppo_sm8250-common).
+> `lineage-24.0` carries the Android 17 bring-up; `lineage-23.2` is the untouched upstream baseline.
+
+## What changed for Android 17
+
+Seven changes, all cross-checked against the official
+[`LineageOS/android_device_oneplus_sm8250-common`](https://github.com/LineageOS/android_device_oneplus_sm8250-common)
+`lineage-24.0` branch (same SM8250 platform):
+
+| Commit | Change | Reason |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Drop TARGET_KERNEL_NO_GCC` | remove one BoardConfig line | Android 17 kernel builds are clang-only, the switch is no longer read |
+| `Switch to the legacy libion implementation` | include `device/lineage/sepolicy/libion/sepolicy.mk` + `soong_config_set_bool(libion, legacy_impl, true)` | libion became configurable; legacy ION ioctl blobs must opt in or sepolicy neverallows block the build |
+| `Drop explicit fastbootd package` | remove `fastbootd` from `PRODUCT_PACKAGES` | pulled in transitively by the fastboot HAL |
+| `Install the recovery init rc as its own module` | `init.oplus.hw.rc.recovery` → `init.oplus.hw.recovery.rc`, new `recovery: true` prebuilt_etc | `recovery_available` no longer installs into the recovery image |
+| `Drop PRODUCT_ENABLE_UFFD_GC` | remove product variable | UFFD GC is the default now |
+| `Update the Bluetooth audio policy include` | `bluetooth_hearing_aid_...xml` → `bluetooth_audio_policy_configuration.xml` | hearing-aid policy merged into the generic BT Audio HAL; the old file no longer exists |
+| `Drop the advanced reboot actions overlay` | remove `config_restartActionsList` | lineage-sdk 24 no longer ships that resource; RROs referencing it fail to compile |
+
+## Status
+
+The patches apply cleanly on `lineage-23.2` (`git am` verified, resulting tree byte-identical
+to the branch). They have **not** been through a full 24.0 compile yet — expect follow-up
+commits for sepolicy and vendor blobs. The full status list lives in `PORTING-24.md`
+of the `device/realme/rivena` tree.
+
+## Building
+
+```bash
+source build/envsetup.sh
+lunch lineage_rivena-userdebug
+m nothing        # config layer: catches most PRODUCT_/BOARD_ breakage
+m sepolicy       # densest error source on old vendor trees
+mka bacon
+```
